# OpenRA Local Dev (Cursor)

This repo is a **local development fork** of OpenRA (Red Alert). It must stay distinguishable from official installs and produce maps that work on [OpenRA Resource Center](https://resource.openra.net/upload/map/) for players who never used this build.

## Git

- **Never `git push` or `git pull`** (or fetch/merge/rebase from remote) unless the user **explicitly** asks in that message.
- **Never create commits** unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not change git config. Avoid destructive git commands unless explicitly requested.

## Maps and `.oramap` compatibility

- Saved maps must be **indistinguishable from maps made in official OpenRA** for upload and play.
- **Do not** add custom fields, metadata, or formats to `Map`, map save logic, or `.oramap` serialization.
- **Editor-only** helpers (rich tile names, search, tooltips, purple UI, dev labels) must **not** change what is written into map files—only what the local editor UI shows.

When placing tiles, maps store official **template IDs** and terrain data from `mods/*/tilesets/*.yaml` (e.g. `sh07.sno` → template id in yaml). Dev tooling may document `Images`, `Categories`, and terrain types for search; the saved file stays vanilla.

## Editor vs game data

- Tile metadata for the intelligent editor: read from existing tileset YAML (`Images`, `Categories`, terrain types). Prefer UI-only changes (`TileSelectorLogic`, chrome, tooltips) over changing core map types.
- Shore/beach tiles use assets like `sh01.sno` … `sh56.sno`; interior walls use `wall0001.int` etc.; outdoor “walls” may be cliffs, beach, or actors (`BRIK`, `FENC`, …)—tileset-dependent.

## Local dev branding (this build only)

- Purple menu/chrome and `[Local Dev]` window title are intentional so this build is not confused with official OpenRA.
- Reapply purple UI after upstream asset pulls: `mods/ra/uibits/apply-dev-purple-theme.ps1` (see `mods/ra/uibits/*.bak`).

## Build

- Target framework: **net8.0** (`Directory.Build.props`). SDK is often user-local at `%USERPROFILE%\.dotnet`.
- If build fails with DLL locked, OpenRA is running—close it or ask before stopping the process.
- Prefer rebuilding after C# editor changes; YAML/chrome changes may hot-reload depending on how the game is launched.

## Code changes

- **Minimize scope**—smallest correct diff; do not refactor unrelated code.
- Match OpenRA/C# conventions in surrounding files.
- Do not add tests or docs unless asked.

- Avoid winget install, they get stuck. Find another way to install.